# Detection: RDP/SMB Brute Force
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1110 (Brute Force)
# Telemetry: Windows Security Event Log (4625 failed logon, 4624 success)
# Logic: multiple failed logons followed by a success from a single source IP.
# Alert: scheduled every 5 min, Last 15 min window (failures + success must
#        fall in the same window), trigger when results > 0, throttle 60 min
#        by Source_Network_Address. Severity: High.
#
# Note: generate the real failure->success pattern with an RDP brute force.
# SMB can log ANONYMOUS LOGON null-session "successes" that are false positives.

index=win-security sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" (EventCode=4625 OR EventCode=4624)
| stats count(eval(EventCode=4625)) AS fails count(eval(EventCode=4624)) AS success by Source_Network_Address
| where fails > 3 AND success > 0
